WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.162
Some numbers pair off exactly.
Others always leave one over.

2
00:00:08.382 --> 00:00:12.190
And some numbers make a perfect
square of dots, like 16.

3
00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:15.755
Take some counters and
pair them off, two by two.

4
00:00:15.975 --> 00:00:21.362
8 makes four whole pairs, and
nothing is left over. So 8 is even.

5
00:00:21.582 --> 00:00:26.365
Now try 7. It makes three pairs
and one left over, so 7 is odd.

6
00:00:26.585 --> 00:00:30.300
That one left over is the whole
story. Watch what it does next.

7
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.026
Add 7 and 5. Both are odd,
so each one has a leftover.

8
00:00:35.246 --> 00:00:39.844
Put them together. The two leftovers
find each other and make a pair.

9
00:00:40.064 --> 00:00:45.358
So 7 add 5 is 12, and 12 is even.
Two odd numbers make an even one.

10
00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:49.943
Taking away follows the same
rule. 9 take away 3 leaves 6.

11
00:00:50.163 --> 00:00:54.668
Both leftovers cancel, so 6
pairs up exactly. It is even too.

12
00:00:55.168 --> 00:00:59.162
A shape in a sum stands for a
number nobody has told you yet.

13
00:00:59.382 --> 00:01:03.933
15 add triangle is 22. The
triangle has to fill the gap.

14
00:01:04.153 --> 00:01:10.144
22 take away 15 is 7, so the triangle
must be 7. It is not a guess.

15
00:01:10.364 --> 00:01:16.354
Sometimes the shape comes first, in a
take-away: triangle take away 14 is 30.

16
00:01:16.574 --> 00:01:23.912
Put the two parts back together: 30
add 14 is 44. The triangle is 44.

17
00:01:24.412 --> 00:01:27.988
A sequence follows a rule
from one term to the next one.

18
00:01:28.208 --> 00:01:33.409
Look at 5, 12, 19, 26. Take each
term away from the one after it.

19
00:01:33.629 --> 00:01:40.874
Every step is add 7, the same each time. That
makes it linear, and the next term is 33.

20
00:01:41.094 --> 00:01:48.106
Now look at 2, 5, 9, 14. The steps
are add 3, then add 4, then add 5.

21
00:01:48.326 --> 00:01:55.431
Those steps change every time, so it is non-linear.
The rule is to add one more than before.

22
00:01:55.931 --> 00:02:00.483
A square number is one you can lay
out as a perfect square of dots.

23
00:02:00.703 --> 00:02:05.625
Here are 4 rows of 4 dots. Count
them: that is 16 altogether.

24
00:02:05.845 --> 00:02:09.885
So 16 is a square number.
We write it as 4 squared.

25
00:02:10.105 --> 00:02:14.610
It means a number times
itself: 4 times 4 is 16, not 8.

26
00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:19.892
The first four square numbers are
1, 4, 9 and 16. Look at them grow.

27
00:02:20.392 --> 00:02:24.247
To grow a square by one, you
add a whole L along two edges.

28
00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:29.575
A 6 by 6 square needs 6 new dots
down the side and 6 along the bottom.

29
00:02:29.795 --> 00:02:34.160
And one more in the corner, where
the two arms meet. That makes 13.

30
00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:42.832
6 times 6 is 36, and 7 times 7 is 49.
The gap is 13, just as we counted.

31
00:02:43.052 --> 00:02:48.161
Every L is the next odd number:
3, then 5, then 7, then 9.

32
00:02:48.661 --> 00:02:53.444
Even numbers pair off exactly.
Odd numbers always leave one over.

33
00:02:53.664 --> 00:02:57.565
Two odd numbers, added or taken
away, give you an even one.

34
00:02:57.785 --> 00:03:01.779
A shape hides a number, and a
sequence follows a rule you can say.

35
00:03:01.999 --> 00:03:06.596
And a square number really does make
a square of dots. Go and build one.
